1. GRANT OF LICENSE
pdprobe (and its pdctl alias and libpdprobe.a library) is distributed under two tiers:
(a) Free Core Tier: USB-C host and tester discovery (probe), USB-PD PDO/RDO
    auditing (audit), live and fixture telemetry (telemetry), safe 5V rollback
    (reset), --dry-run trigger validation, --describe, --help, --version, and
    the stdio MCP server (mcp) for read-only and dry_run=true tool calls.
(b) Commercial Pro Tier ($29 USD one-time perpetual Polar.sh license, up to 3
    personal machines): live hardware PD/PPS/EPR-AVS triggering via `pdprobe
    trigger` and `trigger_pd_pps` (`dry_run: false`). Open-source builds
    compiled with `-DOSS_EDITION` unlock all capabilities offline with no
    license checks.

